## Hard Rules
- After EVERY file edit: run [typecheck command]. FORBIDDEN from reporting "Done" until it passes.
- Before EVERY edit: re-read the file. After EVERY edit: read again to confirm.
- Files over 500 LOC: MUST read in chunks. NEVER assume single read = complete.
- Max 5 files per phase. State phase plan. Wait for approval between phases.
- After 10+ messages: re-read files before editing. Trust nothing from memory.
- If search returns few results: re-run narrower. State truncation suspicion.
- On ANY rename: search direct calls, type refs, string literals, dynamic imports,
  re-exports, barrel files, test mocks SEPARATELY.
- If architecture is flawed: propose structural fixes, not band-aids.
- NEVER create /core, /utils, /helpers folders unless already established.
